RagoShell changelog
===================

RagoShell 2.1.0
---------------
- Keyboard shortcuts are written for the platform and shown only where they work: the Command key (⌘) on a Mac and an
  iPad, Ctrl elsewhere, and on a phone or tablet only while a hardware keyboard is attached (a tablet no longer
  says "Ctrl+L"); the Welcome texts name the gesture on a touch screen
- Control sizes follow the device: desktop, tablet (smaller than before) and phone columns; two-column forms stack on
  narrow screens, tab bars and toolbars no longer cover or cut their buttons (toolbars scroll sideways), the Test
  Connection bar holds its button, and dialogs, the shell tab and the Server Monitor fit a 360 dp phone; the tab
  strip shows every tab in Arabic
- New application icons for every platform (Windows, macOS Big Sur grid, Linux icon theme, Android adaptive and
  themed, iPad light / dark / tinted), all made from one artwork by `dev/icons/make-icons.sh`
- The JavaScript shell runs inside the app (Qt's JavaScript engine) on every platform and the app no longer
  needs a Node.js process for it; the shell works on Android tablets and on the iPad. What changes for you:
  a server result can be used in the same statement (`for (...) { var d = db.c.findOne(...); ... }` and
  `db.c.countDocuments({}) > 0` work as in the old mongo shell), `NumberLong` keeps every digit, a `print`
  statement no longer shows an extra `1`, Stop also ends a long server operation (killOp) and the shell
  timeout stops a script that loops. Output formats, the startup script and autocomplete are unchanged.
  The packages no longer contain Node.js (about 77 MB less), a shell tab needs a tenth of the memory and
  connects about three times as fast, and the old Node shell, its `--shell-backend` switch and
  `src/rago-shell/` are removed
- Log file: ragoshell.log in the settings folder's logs/ directory (5 MB,
  one rotated file) with the app's log lines and all Qt messages;
  Help -> Open Log Folder opens it
- The window layout (splitter sizes, log panel, explorer) is saved a second
  after it changes, so a crash or forced shutdown keeps it
- Unsaved script text of shell tabs is kept as drafts; after a crash or a
  forced shutdown File -> Recover Unsaved Scripts (offered at startup) opens
  them in new tabs, connecting only when you click
- The key that encrypts saved passwords and API keys moves into the operating
  system key store (Windows Credential Manager, macOS Keychain, Linux Secret
  Service) on first start and the key file is removed; without a key store the
  file stays, with a warning in Preferences. An older RagoShell started
  afterwards cannot read the saved passwords
- SSH tunnels check the server's host key against ssh/known_hosts: a new key
  asks for confirmation (SHA256 fingerprint), a changed key is refused
  unless you choose Trust New Key
- SSH tunnels work again: libssh2 1.11.1 (vcpkg) replaces the in-tree 1.9.0,
  which failed every handshake with OpenSSL 3
- Importing and exporting collections reads and writes in batches: memory
  use no longer grows with the file (CSV export reads the collection twice)
- The page size is limited to 1000 documents
- The background schema analysis waits while the network is metered
  (Preferences switch, on by default) and, on tablets, while the app is not in
  front
- After the network comes back or the computer wakes the open connections are
  checked by themselves; errors in that time go to the status bar
- Interface density (Preferences): Automatic, Compact or Touch sizes for
  buttons, fields and menu items; the window can be as narrow as 480 px (the
  explorer folds away, the Welcome page and toolbar adapt); result cells open
  their menu on press-and-hold with a finger; F10 also answers to Alt+Shift+O
- The connection dialog offers only the authentication mechanisms the build
  supports
- Preferences shows where the API key of the AI assistant comes from
- RAGOSHELL_CONFIG_DIR now also moves the query history and the schema
  catalog
- Groundwork for Android tablets (not released): build presets for Android
  and iPadOS, the key for saved passwords is protected by the Android
  Keystore, and the app asks for the local network permission that Android 17
  requires before connecting to a server on the LAN
- Dialogs follow the on-screen keyboard on tablets: they size and center themselves in the space the
  keyboard leaves, and the connection and preferences forms scroll to the field you are typing in
- The "Load ~/.mongorc.js" switch is replaced by a "Startup script" box in Preferences
  (JavaScript that runs before every query in a shell tab); a switched-on old setting copies
  your ~/.mongorc.js into the box once. Nothing reads files from the home folder any more
- Shell tabs have an action strip above the editor (Format, History, Snippets, Export, Query
  Bar, Find and a menu) that adapts to the width of the tab
- New top bar: one row with a search field (the command palette), New Connection,
  Monitor, a theme button and a "more" menu; the menu bar and the row of buttons are
  gone (every command is in the command palette); the same on every platform
- Command palette (Ctrl+K, or Tools -> Command Palette): search every command, saved
  connection and loaded database or collection; recently used commands come first and
  unavailable commands say what they need
- Icons that use Unicode symbols no longer show as empty boxes on Android
  (a symbol font is bundled in the mobile builds; three rarely supported
  symbols were replaced everywhere)

RagoShell 2.0.0
---------------
First RagoShell release. Rebranded continuation of the open-source
Robomongo 1.4.4 codebase with a modernized toolchain:

- Qt 6.12 and CMake presets / vcpkg manifest mode
- Qt Quick (QML) user interface (ragoshell) on a GUI-free core
  library; the Qt Widgets UI has been removed (last commit with it is
  tagged widgets-final)
- Official mongo-cxx-driver 4.0.0 (bsoncxx/mongocxx) replacing legacy
  mongo:: driver APIs
- JavaScript shell moved to a bundled Node.js helper (src/rago-shell,
  mongodb@6.16 driver) over a JSON line protocol; a real node/node.exe is
  shipped inside packages, no separate Node.js install required
- Lighter startup: QtWebEngine welcome tab replaced by a lightweight
  network implementation
- Bounded output log to prevent memory growth in long sessions
- mongoexport path no longer hard-coded; searched next to the app or
  on PATH
- Config directory is ~/.ragoshell/
- Server compatibility: MongoDB 3.6 - 7.x (4.0 verified)
- Local CI packaging scripts for Windows x64, Linux x64, macOS arm64
- 15 UI languages (English, Hindi, Chinese (Simplified), Spanish, Portuguese
  (Brazil), Russian, German, French, Japanese, Arabic, Turkish, Azerbaijani,
  Kazakh, Kyrgyz, Uzbek) with a language picker in Preferences (live switch,
  default follows the OS), right-to-left layout for Arabic, plural forms and
  per-language fallback fonts; translations are machine drafts awaiting
  native review (docs/Localization.md)
